<http://data.silknow.org/object/3c18d44d-3a69-37ed-934b-df8e21517299>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Valance of heavy-quality diapered linen with an applied silk ribbon and fringe. Backed with two layers of coarse linen and a lining of cream silk. Edged all round with applied pale blue silk ribbon. Ribbon forms a pattern of curved shapes following contours of scalloped edges. Bottom edge has an applied woven braid in beige silk with a long fringe. Label attached with 'J. H. INC.'."@en , "Valance of linen applied with silk ribbon and fringe, Germany, ca. 1756-1775"@en ;
